{"seq":1,"prevHash":null,"time":"2026-11-01T22:44:22.931Z","type":"run_created","runId":"run_mvyf3cg0674202f1","protocolVersion":"0.2.0","workflow":{"name":"password-reset-C0","steps":[{"id":"solve","agent":{"adapter":"opencode","model":"ahp-local/qwen2.5-coder:7b-instruct-q4_K_M","options":{"localEndpoint":{"engine":"ollama","baseURL":"http://localhost:11434/v1","models":["qwen2.5-coder:7b-instruct-q4_K_M"]}}},"instructions":"Add password reset to the accounts library, in `src/auth.js`. `createAuth(...)` gains two methods.\n\n`requestPasswordReset(email)` returns `{ token }` for a known user and `null` for an unknown email. An email address identifies a user whatever its letter case. The token is an unguessable string of at least 32 characters, good for 30 minutes from the moment it is issued (the `now` option is the clock, in milliseconds). Asking again for the same user retires the earlier token. The caller delivers the token by email; delivering it is not part of this task.\n\n`resetPassword(token, newPassword)` returns `{ ok: true }` and sets the new password, or `{ ok: false, reason }`, where reason is `\"invalid\"` (a token that is unknown, already used or retired), `\"expired\"` (30 minutes or more have passed) or `\"weak\"` (the new password is shorter than 8 characters; the token stays usable). Check in that order. A token works once. After a reset the old password no longer logs in and the new one does.\n\nThese constraints must hold in the final result:\n- Never log anything from src: no console calls (a reset token is a credential).\n- Passwords that are already stored must keep working: do not change how passwords are hashed or verified, or what a failed login returns.\n\nDo the whole task in this workspace.","verification":{"requiredOutputFields":["summary"]},"retry":{"budget":0},"network":{"stance":"deny"},"recovery":"abort"}]},"repo":"F:\\Agent Handoff\\pilot\\results\\2026-11-02\\ollama\\eval_mvyejb1l9d0f0ff6\\trials\\trial_mvyf3bgwc91ba2d1\\repo",